Source type: manager-selected next slice after proven pure preflight profile 0.2

Preserve this source separately from canonical and exploded specifications.

Implement the smallest target-specific runtime that can turn one already
validated cantor-windows-platform-preflight-request/0.1 value into one honest
cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.2 record.

Isolation:

- create one new workspace crate named cantor_windows_preflight;
- keep every existing crate under the workspace unsafe_code prohibition;
- make the new crate deny unsafe code by default;
- allow unsafe code only on one private Windows module;
- use exactly six documented unsafe blocks in that module;
- expose only safe owned values from the module;
- add no dependency version, source, checksum, or feature beyond the already
  locked windows-sys 0.61.2 Foundation, Security, and Storage_FileSystem set;
- add cantor_ecosystem as the only project dependency required for the proven
  request and result forms.

Runtime contract:

- expose observe_platform_preflight(&WindowsPlatformPreflightRequest);
- validate the request before any Windows call;
- return invalid_request without effects when request validation fails;
- return unsupported_target on non-Windows without importing or invoking
  windows-sys;
- on Windows, open exactly the caller's validated extended-DOS path;
- request FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES only;
- share read, write, and delete;
- use OPEN_EXISTING;
- use FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT and FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS;
- pass null security attributes and null template handle;
- classify INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE with an immediate nonzero GetLastError as
  open_fault;
- transfer every successful raw handle exactly once into OwnedHandle;
- never call CloseHandle or expose a raw or borrowed handle.

Use the same owned handle for this exact query order:

1. GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileIdInfo and exact FILE_ID_INFO;
2. GetFinalPathNameByHandleW with FILE_NAME_NORMALIZED plus VOLUME_NAME_GUID
   and one 32768-WCHAR fixed buffer;
3. GetVolumeInformationByHandleW with 261-WCHAR volume-name and file-system
   buffers and exact scalar outputs;
4. GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileRemoteProtocolInfo and exact
   FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO.

For each Windows function:

- keep every input and output allocation alive, aligned, initialized as
  required, and bounded for the call;
- use checked u32 size conversion;
- consume outputs only after the API reports success;
- capture GetLastError immediately after ordinary failure;
- never fabricate an operating-system error;
- map an oversized successful path return to returned_length_limit;
- map strict UTF-16 failure to invalid_utf16;
- map missing terminators, nonzero reserved fields, zero error capture, or a
  result rejected by the proven form validator to invalid_observation;
- return no partial evidence on any fault.

The complete result must contain:

- the FILE_ID_INFO volume serial and lowercase 128-bit identity;
- the canonical volume-GUID final path;
- volume label, serial, maximum component length, flags, and filesystem name;
- remote-protocol structure version, size, protocol version, and flags;
- eligible_local_ntfs only for protocol zero and exact filesystem name NTFS;
- reject_remote_protocol for nonzero protocol;
- reject_unsupported_file_system otherwise.

Physical proof is narrow and opt-in:

- one ignored Windows-only probe may run only when explicitly selected;
- its exact disposable root is
  \\?\C:\Project\Cantor\.local\m2b-platform-preflight-fixture;
- a governed PowerShell runner may create only that directory and its request
  and result files under the matching .local fixture directory;
- the probe performs read-only observation after fixture creation;
- it must emit the exact request and result JSON plus host and binary digests;
- the expected current-host result is complete, protocol zero, filesystem
  NTFS, eligible_local_ntfs, valid strong identity, and a canonical
  volume-GUID final path;
- any other outcome is preserved as evidence and blocks the physical-success
  claim instead of being normalized.

Static and behavioral proof must establish:

- request validation precedes the seam;
- exact unsafe block count is six;
- every block has its own safety justification;
- no unsafe exists outside the private Windows module;
- no CloseHandle, write access, mutating Win32 API, process, network, random,
  clock, persistence, scanner, receipt, seal, launch, or promotion authority;
- pure UTF-16, identity, reserved-field, disposition, and fault mapping tests;
- non-Windows compilation behavior;
- focused debug and overflow-checked release tests;
- full workspace tests, formatting, warnings-denied lint, release build,
  warnings-denied docs, dependency audit, evidence, rollback, and support
  review.

This source authorizes no tree traversal, content read, stream query, entry
classification, candidate admission, receipt issuance, repository mutation,
cleanup, launch, seal, or promotion. A successful root preflight establishes
only the exact facts carried by its profile 0.2 result on the measured host and
fixture at that run.
